{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-101729",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3p)}{5-3p} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-11}{5-3p} \\\\  & =\\frac{-19}{5-3p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we know that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=-2$ on the interval $[3p,5].$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\frac{-19}{5-3p}=-2.\n$$\n\nSolving for $p,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-19}{5-3p} & =-2 \\\\ -19 & =-2\\cdot (5-3p) \\\\ -19 & =-10+6p \\\\ -19+10 & =6p \\\\ -9 & =6p \\\\ \\frac{-9}{6} & =\\frac{6p}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & =p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $p=-\\frac{3}{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
